# --- s019 Book I d.3 q.4 (= Ord. I d.3 p.1 q.4, nn. 202–280: illumination)
n("n367","s019-01","Quarta questio distinctionis tertie","la","commentary","= *Ord.* I d. 3 p. 1 q. 4 (Vatican III, nn. 202–280), Scotus's question on divine illumination. The wording of the question matches n. 202 verbatim (*an aliqua veritas certa et sincera possit naturaliter cognosci ab intellectu viatoris, absque lucis increatae speciali illustratione*).","verified")
n("n368","s019-01","p°. de tri. c. 6. et 15","la","textual","A clearly prints *p°.* (B agrees in substance). Scotus has *IX De Trinitate cap. 6 vel 15* (*Ord.* I d. 3 n. 202), and the quotation is from Aug. *De Trin.* IX 6.9. *p°* is very probably a misreading of a numeral *9°* in Gorris's exemplar or by the compositor. The English corrects it.","certain")
n("n369","s019-01","Intuemur imutabilem veritatem ex qua perfecte cum possumus diffiniamus","la","source","Aug. *De Trin.* IX 6.9 (*intuemur inviolabilem veritatem, ex qua perfecte, quantum possumus, definiamus…*). Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 3 n. 202, has *inviolabilem*. *imutabilem* is a slip of memory or an exemplar variant, and *cum* stands for *quantum*.","verified")
n("n370","s019-01","hec inuisibilia per visibilia cognoscuntur","la","source","Rom. 1:20 (*invisibilia enim ipsius… per ea quae facta sunt intellecta conspiciuntur*), paraphrased. It is the *ad oppositum* of the Vatican text: *Ord.* I d. 3 n. 203 app.","certain")
n("n371","s019-02","opinio Henrici in summa articulo. 1.","la","source","Henry of Ghent, *Summa* a. 1 q. 2 (*utrum homo possit aliquid scire sine divina illustratione*), set out by Scotus at *Ord.* I d. 3 nn. 204–217. Gorris's one-line summary (being can be known *sub ratione entis*, not *sub ratione veritatis*) is Henry's distinction between knowing the *verum* and knowing the *veritas* of a thing.","verified")
n("n372","s019-02","quodlibeto. 5. q. 14","la","source","Henry, *Quodl.* V q. 14, so also in B (*q. xiiij*). The link Gorris makes to Scotus's second article (*Ord.* I d. 3 nn. 229ff., against the Academics) has not been traced in the Vatican apparatus.","to-verify")
n("n373","s019-02","questione⟨m quod pro⟩ter verba","la","textual","A is stained at the top right of p. 34. Supplied from B (fol. 32ra: *Igitur dico ad questionem quod propter verba etc.*), which agrees with *Ord.* I d. 3 n. 261: *Ad quaestionem igitur dico quod propter verba Augustini…*","verified")
n("n374","s019-02","E⟨x dictis⟩ patet ad omnes auctoritates Aug. in oppositum","la","textual","Stain in A. Supplied from B (*Ex dictis patet ad omnes auctoritates Aug. in oppositum*). The words are the last sentence of *Ord.* I d. 3 n. 279.","verified")
n("n375","s019-02","sextus vero ⟨ar⟩ticulus de communi non reperitur in libris","la","commentary","An important witness to the state of the text. At n. 218 Scotus announces six articles, the sixth to show *quomodo rationes istae quatenus sunt Augustini concludunt*. In the Vatican edition the sixth article (n. 280) breaks off after its opening sentence (*De sexto articulo videndum est… Ubi sciendum est.*). Gorris's remark that it 'is not found in the books' therefore matches the surviving tradition exactly: Scotus left it unwritten. ⟨ar⟩ and ⟨c e⟩ (in *si⟨c e⟩um*) are supplied from B (*Sextus vero articulus de omni non reperitur in libris. et sic eum non posui*). B's *de omni* (probably for *omnino*) differs from A's *de communi*. I take A's phrase as 'in the common books' (i.e. the copies in circulation), but the construction is odd.","certain")
n("n376","s019-03","ly in potest capi obiectiue et hoc quadrupliciter","la","source","*Ord.* I d. 3 n. 261, verbatim apart from word order. The four modes are expounded in nn. 262 (first), 263 (second), 264–266 (third) and 277 (fourth, *in obiecto remoto*). Gorris's comment on the 'fourth' mode, however, gives the doctrine of n. 267f. (secondary objects have only *esse secundum quid*, so they move only by virtue of the divine intellect). That doctrine belongs to the third mode in Scotus.","verified")
n("n377","s019-03","Aug. 9. de trini.","la","source","Scotus cites *De Trinitate* XIV c. 15 (*Ord.* I d. 3 n. 263; Aug. *De Trin.* XIV 15.21: *ubi ergo sunt istae regulae scriptae nisi in libro lucis illius quae veritas dicitur?*). A's *9.* (B *ix* or similar) is an error, perhaps carried over from the IX cited in the opening argument. The English corrects it.","verified")
n("n378","s019-03","obiecta secundaria in esse intelligibili","la","commentary","Scotus's doctrine of the divine ideas as *obiecta secundaria* of the divine intellect, produced in *esse intelligibile* or *esse deminutum* (*Ord.* I d. 3 n. 262; cf. d. 35 q. un.). It is Scotus's reinterpretation of Augustinian illumination, without any special influence.","certain")
n("n379","s019-03","Et hoc secundum modum","la","textual","A has an abbreviation (*ʒ⁹* with a *z*-form). It is read as *secundum*, giving the sense 'and this [is] the second mode'. It could also be *scilicet*.","uncertain")
n("n380","s019-04","Aug. 4°. de tri. c. 35.","la","source","Aug. *De Trin.* IV 15.20. Gorris's 'ch. 35' is not an error of his own. It reproduces Scotus's medieval chapter numbering (*Ord.* I d. 3 n. 270: *IV De Trinitate cap. 35*). The quotation follows Scotus closely, but Gorris has *nondum potuisse venire* where Scotus and Augustine have *nondum posse*.","verified")
n("n381","s019-05","12. de tri. c. 4.","la","source","Aug. *De Trin.* XII 14.23, cited by Scotus as *XII De Trinitate cap. 14* (*Ord.* I d. 3 n. 273). A's *c. 4* has lost a digit.","verified")
n("n382","s019-05","octuaginta trium questionum. q. 46.","la","source","Aug. *De div. qu. 83*, q. 46.2 (*De ideis*): *non nisi purae animae*. Cited by Scotus at *Ord.* I d. 3 n. 273.","verified")
n("n383","s019-05","iniustus videt in regulis eternis quid iustum sit faciendum","la","source","Aug. *De Trin.* XIV 15.21, via *Ord.* I d. 3 n. 274 (*XIV De Trinitate cap. 15*). Gorris then reduces Scotus's *non tantum ut relucent in phantasmate* to *non tamen*.","verified")
n("n384","s019-06","Aug. locutus est inquirendo non autem determinando","la","commentary","This reply is not in *Ord.* I d. 3 q. 4 as edited, and I have not found it in Scotus's text. It looks like a scholastic commonplace for setting aside an awkward Augustinian dictum. The source (a later Scotist, or Gorris himself) is still to be identified.","to-verify")
n("n385","s019-06","obiectum proximum nobis respectu veritatum sunt obiecta secundaria","la","commentary","Gorris's summary: the proximate object of our knowing the eternal truths is the *obiecta secundaria* (the divine ideas, in their *esse intelligibile*). This differs from Scotus's own cautious statement at nn. 262 and 268, which allows only that we 'may be said' to see in them. The tension between this note and the solution in ¶4 (knowledge *per ista sensibilia*) is Gorris's, not Scotus's.","conjecture")
n("n386","s019-02","not found in the books in common use","en","translation","A *de communi*, B *de omni*. The translation interprets A. See note on the Latin.","uncertain")
n("n387","s019-05","ad rationes intelligibiles","la","textual","Bibliographical note. The foot of p. 35 is signed *c. ij*, with the numeral in the *z*-shaped form. P. 31 is signed *c. i*, and p. 33 carries no signature. If pp. 31–35 are consecutive pages, as the continuous text shows, p. 35 should be c.iii. Either the signature is misprinted or I have misread it. To be checked against the physical copy or a collation formula.","uncertain")
# --- B collation (full): B32L–B33L
n("n1089","s019-01","certa et sincera","la","textual","B: *certa vel sincera*.","certain")
upd("n369", append=" B: *perfecte cum possumus diffamamus* (sic), a misprint.")
upd("n371", append=" B: *ponitur Hen. in sum. arti. i. qui ponit* (without *opinio*).")
n("n1090","s019-03","vel sicut in obiecto proximo","la","textual","B: *Vel sicut in subiecto primo*. In the next two members B also reads *obiectum primum* for A's *obiectum proximum*. A agrees with Scotus (*Ord.* I d. 3 n. 261: *obiecto proximo*).","certain")
n("n1091","s019-03","habent esse intelligibile","la","textual","B: *habent intelligi*.","certain")
upd("n379", append=" B prints the same abbreviation.")
n("n1092","s019-03","non competit alicui precise enti","la","textual","B: *non competit precise enti* (without *alicui*).","certain")
n("n1093","s019-03","mouere intellectum per se nisi","la","textual","B: *mouere intellectum precise nisi*.","certain")
upd("n385", append=" B: *obiectum primum nobis*.")
